WEBVTT

NOTE Captions match the narration. Times follow the spoken words.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.020
This Personal project uses app-managed
storage and starts without a Git

2
00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:06.500
repository.

3
00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:11.373
Personal projects keep the
same project-specific memory,

4
00:00:11.373 --> 00:00:14.320
routines and usage views.

5
00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:18.310
Its execution device owns the storage.

6
00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:21.910
Extra folders and
repositories are optional.

7
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:26.870
Add an existing synthetic folder
and save its access grant.

8
00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:29.670
This does not move the folder.

9
00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:33.407
A repository URL can
coexist with that folder.

10
00:00:33.407 --> 00:00:37.060
Associate the owned local
checkout before saving.

11
00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:40.986
Match checks the checkout's
actual remote identity.

12
00:00:40.986 --> 00:00:44.360
This walkthrough performs
no network clone.

13
00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:47.480
Save a local MCP command separately.

14
00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:51.520
This example is an owned,
inert discovery fixture.

15
00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:53.986
Check discovers MCP tools.

16
00:00:53.986 --> 00:00:58.860
It does not verify a Gmail, Calendar
or other external service account.

17
00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:02.809
Choose and save exactly the
tools this project may use.

18
00:01:02.809 --> 00:01:06.420
Calls still follow
SpecWithCode's approval rules.

19
00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:09.142
Revoke removes future access.

20
00:01:09.142 --> 00:01:13.700
Restoring requires a new discovery
check and fresh tool grants.

21
00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:16.740
The command runs as the device's user.

22
00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:21.633
No external account or AI provider
was contacted in this walkthrough.
